mutation M20 (src/block_agg.c)
broken guard: plan(): MERGE requires last < to instead of last <= to, so a block ending exactly at `to` decodes instead of merging. Conservative, so the numbers stay right -- what goes red is the vacuity ledger's merge/seam counters, which is the point: a 'safe' plan that stops merging is a phase that stopped working.
expected to be caught by: sec5

--- if (id->first_timestamp_ns >= from_mono_ns &&
        id->last_timestamp_ns <= to_mono_ns)
        return PGWT_BLOCK_MERGE;
+++ if (id->first_timestamp_ns >= from_mono_ns &&
        id->last_timestamp_ns < to_mono_ns)
        return PGWT_BLOCK_MERGE;   /* MUTANT: half-open containment */

